cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use portparity in research or a migration project, please cite it as below."
title: "portparity: differential behavior testing for code migration with AI agents"
abstract: >-
  portparity is an agent skill for Claude Code and Codex, plus a dependency-free Python runner,
  for behavior-preserving code migration. It runs an original implementation (the oracle) and its
  replacement on the same JSON inputs through language-neutral adapters, compares results strictly,
  shrinks mismatches to minimal regression cases while preserving the failure type, validates the
  harness with negative controls and determinism checks, and writes an evidence report that states
  its scope and limitations.
type: software
